# Scenario for scripts/record-scenario.py: the Z8001 mandelbrot,
# segmented -- its code in segment 1, its variables in segment 2 -- runs
# in normal mode on a stack in segment 4, doing its I/O by SC into system
# code whose stack is in segment 3. Its arithmetic is inline MULT and DIV,
# which take a 32-bit register pair: DIV leaves the quotient in the low
# word and the remainder in the high word. Load it, break at each frame's
# end, disassemble the inner loop, run up to its first DIV and single-step
# it on the chip, then let the frame finish.
#
# ADDRESSES ARE PINNED TO THE CURRENT samples/z8001/mandelbrot.hex, as
# seg<<16|off: 1012A is the `sc #SC_NEWLINE` right after mandelbrot()
# returns -- once per frame, so a breakpoint there turns every 'G' into
# "run exactly one frame"; 10172 is loop_i, 10178 its first DIV. If
# mandelbrot.asm/.inc change, re-check them against the fresh
# mandelbrot.lst before recording.

key R
upload samples/z8001/mandelbrot.hex
# Reset again: the FCW and PC come from the program just loaded, whose
# FCW says whether to decode it segmented.
key R

# A breakpoint right after each frame finishes drawing: every 'G' from
# here on runs exactly one frame.
type B
wait Break addr?
command 1012A
pace 0.6

# The inner loop: EXTS sign-extends B into RR2, DIV divides all 32 bits
# of it by F.
type D
wait Disassemble?
command 10172
pace 1.5

# Up to the DIV, then a few steps on the chip: the quotient Q in R3, the
# remainder S in R2, stored to their variables.
type g
wait Go until?
command 10178 4
pace 0.9
step 4
pace 1.2

# The rest of the frame, live.
command G 10
pace 1.2
